"""
Auto Question Generator — Multi-Provider NEET/JEE edition
------------------------------------------------------
Features:
- Choose ONE provider per run: OmniRoute (self-hosted OpenAI-
  compatible proxy), Agent Router (agentrouter.org, hosted), or
  Claude API (Anthropic, native Messages API). Each keeps its own
  API key independently, so switching providers doesn't lose what
  you typed for the others.
- Maximum 50 selected PDF pages per run.
- Maximum 60 questions per run.
- Individual page selection/deselection.
- Questions-per-page and sub-topic for every selected page.
- Mandatory global topic and per-page sub-topics.
- Estimated remaining time below the progress bar.
- Source field equals the uploaded PDF filename.
- NEET/JEE concept-based prompts that reject passage-copying questions.
- Cross-page duplicate and near-duplicate detection (question text AND
  underlying concept), tracked for the whole run rather than reset on
  every page, plus a final safety-net dedup pass before export.
- Each page's prompt is told which concepts earlier pages already
  covered, so it is steered away from re-testing the same fact.
- Explanation/answer-key consistency check: rejects questions whose
  explanation second-guesses itself or argues for an option other than
  the stored key.
- Response token budget scales with how many questions a page
  requests, and a truncated/invalid JSON response is retried with a
  larger budget (then salvaged for any complete questions it can
  find) instead of failing the whole page outright.
- Difficulty is explicitly decoupled from question length in the
  prompt — "Hard" means conceptually tricky, not a longer sentence.
- MCQ/Numerical question types.
- Optional PER-PAGE source-figure attachment: when a question is
  genuinely about a figure/diagram the source PDF page already
  contains, that REAL image is extracted from the page and embedded
  in the Word document right after the question — nothing is drawn
  or invented by the model.
- Full JEE/NEET symbol & formula support: Greek letters, calculus and
  set-theory/logic operators, reaction/equilibrium arrows (with
  \\xrightarrow conditions), vectors/hats/dots, blackboard-bold
  number sets, ion-charge and isotope notation, degrees/primes.
- Fractions and roots (including nth roots) render as real Word EQ
  fields — a stacked fraction and a radical sign with a full bar over
  the whole expression, not flat "3/4" text or a "cropped"-looking √.
- Optional source-page image analysis for image/diagram questions.

Install:
    pip install -r requirements.txt
"""

